assets/original_shader.blend contains editable native base-rendering paths derived
from the Festivity graphs. All images and preview objects were removed; image
nodes retain the original reference names. assets/original_controls.blend contains
the procedural lighting controls and head reference objects.
upstream_mapping.py extracts the original V3_MaterialDataApplier dictionaries.
tools/fetch_upstream.py, build_shader_library.py and build_upstream_mappings.py
describe how these assets and mappings are obtained and prepared. See
assets/upstream.json for input versions and SHA256 provenance.

Better FBX operator integration follows the interface documented in
PaoloESAN/gacha-setup (local reference 3.8.3, utils/better_fbx_utils.py):
https://github.com/PaoloESAN/gacha-setup
Better FBX itself is a separately installed dependency and is not bundled.

Per-character ownership and resource isolation were informed by
AstraMorningstar/Morningstar-Festivity-render-assistant (local reference 1.0.2.1,
character_system.py):
https://github.com/AstraMorningstar/Morningstar-Festivity-render-assistant

Hoyo-GI-Toon adapts the current Blender API and scopes the original setup to each
imported character. It does not distribute game character models, textures,
material dumps or private validation projects. Local game assets are read from
the selected character package.
